{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The default Empty\/Loading\/Error placeholders’ text — “Nothing Here,” “Loading,” “Retry,” “Something Went Wrong,” “Connection Issue” — comes from a String Catalog, ","type":"text"},{"code":"Resources\/Localizable.xcstrings","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", resolved from ScreenStates’ own bundle (","type":"text"},{"code":"Bundle.module","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") rather than your app’s. That’s deliberate: a custom title your app passes in (see below) is never run back through localization, and a language you add to ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"your own"}]},{"text":" app’s catalog has no effect on these five strings — they only ever resolve against ScreenStates’ bundle. English, Spanish, French, and Russian are built in today.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Adding-a-language-to-ScreenStates","text":"Adding a language to ScreenStates","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This is a change to the package itself, not something a consuming app can do on its own — it needs a PR. Open ","type":"text"},{"code":"Resources\/Localizable.xcstrings","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and add a ","type":"text"},{"code":"localizations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" entry for the new language code under each of the five string keys:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["\"Retry\" : {","  \"comment\" : \"Title of the button that retries loading after an error.\",","  \"localizations\" : {","    \"en\" : { \"stringUnit\" : { \"state\" : \"translated\", \"value\" : \"Retry\" } },","    \"de\" : { \"stringUnit\" : { \"state\" : \"translated\", \"value\" : \"Wiederholen\" } }","  }","}"],"syntax":"json","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every one of the five keys needs an entry for every language — a string present in English but missing a translation elsewhere fails CI (see below). ","type":"text"},{"code":"ScreenStatesStrings.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"‘s doc comments list all five keys and their English text if you’re starting from scratch.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Overriding-text-per-app","text":"Overriding text per-app","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You don’t need a new language, or a PR, to show different text than the built-in default — two options, depending on how much you want to replace:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView(title:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" takes a ","type":"text"},{"code":"title","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" directly, bypassing ","type":"text"},{"code":"Localizable.xcstrings","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" entirely for that one string. Pass your own localized string (from your own app’s String Catalog, ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSLocalizedString","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", whatever) instead of the default:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView(title: String(localized: \"No Results\"))"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ScreenStateDefaultErrorView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has no equivalent for its title or Retry button text today — only the error’s own message is customizable, via ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDisplayableError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For anything else — the Error placeholder’s title, the Retry button’s text, or any text at all in a shape the built-in views don’t expose a parameter for — pass a fully custom placeholder instead of the default one, via ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"empty","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"loading","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"error","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" builder closures (see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") or ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateViewController","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"‘s equivalent. A custom placeholder can still reuse ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/accessibilityAnnouncement","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" so VoiceOver announces transitions with the same wording your custom text uses, instead of the default’s.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/localization"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Localization"},"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"How the default placeholders’ built-in text is localized, how to add a language, and how to show different text instead without touching ScreenStates itself.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Localization","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Accessibility"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation","title":"Related Documentation"}],"references":{"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateStore":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateStore"}],"title":"ScreenStateStore","abstract":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" holder of a screen’s ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","type":"reference"},{"text":", driving both","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"SwiftUI and UIKit consumers from a single source of truth.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatestore","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateStore"}]},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenState/accessibilityAnnouncement":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"accessibilityAnnouncement","abstract":[{"text":"The same text the default placeholders announce to VoiceOver for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this case, reusable by a fully custom placeholder that wants to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"announce transitions with the same wording instead of inventing its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"own. ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for ","type":"text"},{"code":".data","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", since at that point a custom placeholder’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"own content is what VoiceOver should read, not a transition","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"announcement.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstate\/accessibilityannouncement","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/accessibilityAnnouncement","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"accessibilityAnnouncement","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateViewController":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScreenStateViewController","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIViewController"},{"type":"text","text":" base class that owns a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateContainerView"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pinned to the view’s edges and bound to a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"wrapping the boilerplate every UIKit screen using ScreenStates"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"otherwise repeats in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"viewDidLoad()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstateviewcontroller","title":"ScreenStateViewController","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScreenStateViewController","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateViewController"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentat